1
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:08,000
[Queen chewing]

2
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:11,000
I have a duty to fulfill.

3
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:14,000
I have to give birth to the King.

4
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:19,000
I am the Queen.

5
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:22,000
[opening theme music playing]

6
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:28,000
[singer singing in Japanese]

7
00:00:55,000 --> 00:00:59,000
[singer singing in English]

8
00:00:59,000 --> 00:01:01,000
[singer singing in Japanese]

9
00:01:01,000 --> 00:01:05,000
[singer singing in English]

10
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:09,000
[singer singing in Japanese]

11
00:01:21,000 --> 00:01:22,000
[singer singing in English]

12
00:01:23,000 --> 00:01:27,000
[singer singing in Japanese]

13
00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:47,000
UNEASE X AND X SIGHTING

14
00:01:51,000 --> 00:01:52,000
[narrator] After using accompany,

15
00:01:52,000 --> 00:01:56,000
Gon and Killua were transported
to Ging's student,

16
00:01:56,000 --> 00:01:57,000
a man named Kite.

17
00:01:57,000 --> 00:02:01,000
After Gon remembered meeting
Kite when he was very young,

18
00:02:01,000 --> 00:02:05,000
he felt that Ging intended
for this meeting to occur,

19
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:07,000
and his curiosity grew.

20
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:11,000
Hey, so what kind
of work do you do, Kite?

21
00:02:11,000 --> 00:02:13,000
[Kite] Biological surveys.

22
00:02:13,000 --> 00:02:17,000
My main focus is discovering
and researching new species.

23
00:02:17,000 --> 00:02:20,000
For instance, have you heard
of the Camp Tiger?

24
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:22,000
-Huh?
-Can't say that I have.

25
00:02:22,000 --> 00:02:24,000
They've mastered fire.

26
00:02:24,000 --> 00:02:25,000
They use tree branches

27
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:28,000
that were ignited by lightning
as kindling.

28
00:02:28,000 --> 00:02:31,000
Other than certain bipedal magical beasts,

29
00:02:31,000 --> 00:02:33,000
they're the first of their kind,

30
00:02:33,000 --> 00:02:37,000
a wild animal that prefers its meat cooked
as opposed to raw.

31
00:02:37,000 --> 00:02:39,000
Hey, check it out!
They're actually cooking it!

32
00:02:39,000 --> 00:02:41,000
They really are using fire!

33
00:02:41,000 --> 00:02:43,000
So what else is there?

34
00:02:43,000 --> 00:02:45,000
Oh, yeah, I almost forgot.

35
00:02:45,000 --> 00:02:49,000
You said the thing that attacked me
was a Chimera Ant, right?

36
00:02:49,000 --> 00:02:52,000
Yes, the Chimera Ant.

37
00:02:53,000 --> 00:02:56,000
It's under a designated
quarantine, level one.

38
00:02:56,000 --> 00:03:00,000
It's a dangerous insect
that normally no one's allowed to be near.

39
00:03:00,000 --> 00:03:02,000
[Gon] So were you the one
who discovered them?

40
00:03:02,000 --> 00:03:05,000
No, I usually specialize
in larger creatures,

41
00:03:05,000 --> 00:03:08,000
but right now,
I'm investigating these insects.

42
00:03:09,000 --> 00:03:11,000
Something has been bothering me lately.

43
00:03:12,000 --> 00:03:14,000
[both] Uh…

44
00:03:16,000 --> 00:03:17,000
[Kite] As it stands,

45
00:03:17,000 --> 00:03:20,000
it looks like I'll have to move
to a different location now.

46
00:03:21,000 --> 00:03:24,000
I need to make a call,
but I'm not getting a signal here.

47
00:03:25,000 --> 00:03:26,000
A phone call?

48
00:03:26,000 --> 00:03:28,000
[Kite] I'm working with others.

49
00:03:28,000 --> 00:03:30,000
There are seven of us on the team.

50
00:03:31,000 --> 00:03:34,000
I guess I'll just have to wait
for them to show up.

51
00:03:34,000 --> 00:03:37,000
They're all amateurs,
but extremely skilled Hunters.

52
00:03:37,000 --> 00:03:38,000
I'll introduce you to them.

53
00:03:38,000 --> 00:03:41,000
[upbeat music playing]

54
00:03:43,000 --> 00:03:44,000
[man] Huh?

55
00:03:44,000 --> 00:03:45,000
Oh, hey!

56
00:03:45,000 --> 00:03:48,000
Huh? Well, speak of the devil.

57
00:03:51,000 --> 00:03:53,000
[woman] Hey, Kite.
Who are these kids?

58
00:03:53,000 --> 00:03:55,000
Some brand-new friends of mine,

59
00:03:55,000 --> 00:03:57,000
dropped by for a short visit
on their travels.

60
00:03:58,000 --> 00:04:01,000
Is that so?
Nice of you to come all this way.

61
00:04:01,000 --> 00:04:04,000
My name is Spinner Clow, Spin for short.

62
00:04:04,000 --> 00:04:05,000
Pleasure to meet you.

63
00:04:06,000 --> 00:04:07,000
Hi. I'm Gon Freecss.

64
00:04:07,000 --> 00:04:09,000
Nice to meet you, Spin.

65
00:04:10,000 --> 00:04:12,000
Hang on. Freecss?

66
00:04:12,000 --> 00:04:14,000
Wait. Does that mean you're--

67
00:04:14,000 --> 00:04:16,000
Yep. This boy is Ging's son.

68
00:04:17,000 --> 00:04:18,000
-Seriously?
-Seriously?

69
00:04:18,000 --> 00:04:19,000
What about you?

70
00:04:19,000 --> 00:04:20,000
Are you Ging's kid, too?

71
00:04:21,000 --> 00:04:22,000
No. That's just Gon.

72
00:04:22,000 --> 00:04:24,000
My name is Killua Zoldyck.

73
00:04:25,000 --> 00:04:26,000
Zoldyck? Really?

74
00:04:26,000 --> 00:04:28,000
Don't take this the wrong way,

75
00:04:28,000 --> 00:04:31,000
but are you a part of the famous
family of assassins?

76
00:04:32,000 --> 00:04:34,000
Mm-hmm.
That's right, but I quit the business.

77
00:04:34,000 --> 00:04:36,000
That's not all.

78
00:04:36,000 --> 00:04:37,000
They're both professional hunters,

79
00:04:37,000 --> 00:04:39,000
so that makes them your seniors.

80
00:04:40,000 --> 00:04:41,000
[all] Oh, wow!

81
00:04:42,000 --> 00:04:43,000
[bags rustle]

82
00:04:44,000 --> 00:04:46,000
[man] Man, what a surprise!

83
00:04:47,000 --> 00:04:49,000
[Spin] We've conducted
biological surveys with Kite

84
00:04:50,000 --> 00:04:51,000
for three years,

85
00:04:51,000 --> 00:04:54,000
but this is the most incredible
organism we've ever seen!

86
00:04:54,000 --> 00:04:56,000
[laughs] You got that right!

87
00:04:57,000 --> 00:04:59,000
I don't think we finished
introducing ourselves.

88
00:04:59,000 --> 00:05:02,000
My name is Monta Yuras,
but you can just call me Mon.

89
00:05:03,000 --> 00:05:04,000
A pleasure, Mon.

90
00:05:04,000 --> 00:05:06,000
And my name's Stick Dinner.

91
00:05:06,000 --> 00:05:08,000
I handle all the cooking,

92
00:05:08,000 --> 00:05:10,000
on account of my name
being dinner, of course.

93
00:05:10,000 --> 00:05:12,000
[laughs]

94
00:05:12,000 --> 00:05:13,000
[laughs]

95
00:05:13,000 --> 00:05:14,000
Nice to meet you.

96
00:05:14,000 --> 00:05:15,000
That just leaves me.

97
00:05:15,000 --> 00:05:18,000
I'm Banana Kavaro.
Good to meet you.

98
00:05:18,000 --> 00:05:19,000
[dog whimpers]

99
00:05:19,000 --> 00:05:22,000
[barks]

100
00:05:22,000 --> 00:05:25,000
Podungo and Lin complete the team.

101
00:05:25,000 --> 00:05:26,000
Where are they now?

102
00:05:27,000 --> 00:05:29,000
They're both heading
toward the area of the sighting.

103
00:05:29,000 --> 00:05:32,000
[Kite] Those two always move so quickly.

104
00:05:32,000 --> 00:05:35,000
Oh. What you told me
earlier was accurate, Kite.

105
00:05:37,000 --> 00:05:38,000
This thing right here,

106
00:05:38,000 --> 00:05:42,000
it looks exactly like
the claw of a Chimera Ant Queen.

107
00:05:42,000 --> 00:05:43,000
[both gasp]

108
00:05:43,000 --> 00:05:45,000
[Kite] Hmm.

109
00:05:45,000 --> 00:05:47,000
[Mon] We ran
some computer analyses,

110
00:05:47,000 --> 00:05:50,000
and it came back a 99% match.

111
00:05:50,000 --> 00:05:51,000
[Killua] Can I see?

112
00:05:51,000 --> 00:05:52,000
Sure.

113
00:05:54,000 --> 00:05:57,000
So this is a Chimera Ant claw?

114
00:05:57,000 --> 00:05:59,000
It's as big as a human finger.

115
00:05:59,000 --> 00:06:01,000
Does that mean
that there are huge ants?

116
00:06:01,000 --> 00:06:03,000
We're not certain.

117
00:06:03,000 --> 00:06:05,000
[Killua] Could one
have mutated that big?

118
00:06:05,000 --> 00:06:07,000
It is possible,
although it may also belong

119
00:06:08,000 --> 00:06:10,000
to a completely different species.

120
00:06:10,000 --> 00:06:13,000
Regardless, we just don't know right now.

121
00:06:14,000 --> 00:06:16,000
That's why we're investigating.

122
00:06:18,000 --> 00:06:20,000
It all started
with a wonky assignment.

123
00:06:20,000 --> 00:06:22,000
Mr. Wong, not wonky!

124
00:06:22,000 --> 00:06:25,000
He's an official from Kakin, see? [laughs]

125
00:06:26,000 --> 00:06:27,000
What does "Kakin" mean?

126
00:06:28,000 --> 00:06:30,000
[Mon] This place.
It's the name of this country

127
00:06:30,000 --> 00:06:32,000
that's in the middle
of the Azian continent.

128
00:06:33,000 --> 00:06:36,000
We had just completed
a biological survey that they'd requested.

129
00:06:38,000 --> 00:06:40,000
[Wong] Wonderful!

130
00:06:40,000 --> 00:06:44,000
You've all managed to complete
200 years' worth of work for our agency.

131
00:06:44,000 --> 00:06:48,000
I feel just awful that I can't pay you
a bonus for your efforts.

132
00:06:48,000 --> 00:06:52,000
It's fine, Mr. Wong.
We were all happy to do it.

133
00:06:52,000 --> 00:06:54,000
I'm sorry nonetheless.

134
00:06:54,000 --> 00:06:56,000
Instead, I'll be sure
to recommend you and your team

135
00:06:56,000 --> 00:06:59,000
to the other friendly nations
we have relationships with.

136
00:07:00,000 --> 00:07:02,000
Thank you.
We appreciate it.

137
00:07:03,000 --> 00:07:05,000
Oh, yes, one more thing.

138
00:07:05,000 --> 00:07:08,000
Forgive me if I ramble,
but Southernpiece said

139
00:07:08,000 --> 00:07:11,000
they recently acquired a segment
of a very strange species.

140
00:07:12,000 --> 00:07:13,000
-Hmm?
-[Wong] They can't list it,

141
00:07:13,000 --> 00:07:15,000
since it could be
an unregistered creature,

142
00:07:15,000 --> 00:07:17,000
so they would, uh,

143
00:07:17,000 --> 00:07:21,000
rather sell it to a licensed
hunter at a nice price

144
00:07:21,000 --> 00:07:25,000
than have it confiscated
by some government agency.

145
00:07:29,000 --> 00:07:30,000
[beeps]

146
00:07:31,000 --> 00:07:34,000
All right, then. Here we are.

147
00:07:41,000 --> 00:07:42,000
[Kite] Your thoughts, Lin?

148
00:07:43,000 --> 00:07:46,000
[Lin] This clearly belongs
to an unregistered species, yes.

149
00:07:47,000 --> 00:07:48,000
And f-from what I can see,

150
00:07:48,000 --> 00:07:50,000
it resembles a giant insect leg.

151
00:07:51,000 --> 00:07:55,000
B-but no known species have
l-legs that are this large.

152
00:07:56,000 --> 00:07:58,000
It seems the claw
exhibits a number of traits

153
00:07:58,000 --> 00:08:00,000
that aren't found in other insects.

154
00:08:00,000 --> 00:08:01,000
Right.

155
00:08:01,000 --> 00:08:04,000
A leg typically has two claws,
but this has six.

156
00:08:04,000 --> 00:08:08,000
It's almost like the Tarsus evolved
into something like fingers.

157
00:08:09,000 --> 00:08:12,000
[Spin] I know, and this segment is spiny.

158
00:08:12,000 --> 00:08:14,000
Think it could be the tibia?

159
00:08:14,000 --> 00:08:17,000
[Podungo] If we take a sample
with us and study it further,

160
00:08:17,000 --> 00:08:18,000
we can learn a lot more.

161
00:08:18,000 --> 00:08:20,000
So what do you say?

162
00:08:20,000 --> 00:08:21,000
Do you think we could have
a small piece?

163
00:08:22,000 --> 00:08:23,000
Well, I simply can't refuse

164
00:08:23,000 --> 00:08:26,000
anyone who was recommended
to me by Mr. Wong.

165
00:08:29,000 --> 00:08:31,000
[Podungo] Thank you.
We'll look into this.

166
00:08:31,000 --> 00:08:33,000
As soon as we have
all the results back,

167
00:08:33,000 --> 00:08:34,000
we'll let you know.

168
00:08:34,000 --> 00:08:36,000
Mm-hmm. Good luck.

169
00:08:41,000 --> 00:08:42,000
The Chimera Ant.

170
00:08:47,000 --> 00:08:50,000
So where did
Podungo and Lin go off to?

171
00:08:50,000 --> 00:08:53,000
Somewhere south
of Yorknew city, I think.

172
00:08:53,000 --> 00:08:54,000
The person who found the leg

173
00:08:54,000 --> 00:08:57,000
apparently lives in a city
pretty close to the ocean.

174
00:08:58,000 --> 00:08:59,000
[Kite] I realize you just got back,

175
00:08:59,000 --> 00:09:02,000
but we should really hurry after them.

176
00:09:02,000 --> 00:09:05,000
Hey, would it be okay
if we came along with you?

177
00:09:05,000 --> 00:09:06,000
[Kite] Hmm?

178
00:09:06,000 --> 00:09:08,000
Yes, of course.

179
00:09:08,000 --> 00:09:09,000
All right!

180
00:09:10,000 --> 00:09:11,000
Glad to have you.

181
00:09:11,000 --> 00:09:13,000
You mean we'll have
two pro Hunters with us?

182
00:09:13,000 --> 00:09:16,000
Great! That is so reassuring.

183
00:09:16,000 --> 00:09:19,000
And they're Ging's son
and somebody from the Zoldyck family.

184
00:09:19,000 --> 00:09:20,000
Oh, I'm sorry.

185
00:09:20,000 --> 00:09:22,000
Oh, it's no big deal.

186
00:09:22,000 --> 00:09:24,000
[vials clinking]

187
00:09:26,000 --> 00:09:29,000
[Mon] So you kids are
already pros at your age, huh?

188
00:09:29,000 --> 00:09:31,000
[Stick] Well, we weren't born
with the talent ourselves,

189
00:09:32,000 --> 00:09:34,000
but I wish they'd lent that ta-lent to me.

190
00:09:34,000 --> 00:09:36,000
Do you get it? [laughs]

191
00:09:36,000 --> 00:09:39,000
[Gon laughs]

192
00:09:40,000 --> 00:09:43,000
[Kite] They've become friends,
and in such a short time.

193
00:09:45,000 --> 00:09:47,000
Good Hunters
are well liked by animals.

194
00:09:48,000 --> 00:09:51,000
They're often blessed
with good friends as well.

195
00:09:55,000 --> 00:09:58,000
Gon is the real deal.

196
00:09:58,000 --> 00:10:00,000
He's sure
to find you soon enough, Ging.

197
00:10:02,000 --> 00:10:05,000
[ominous music playing]

198
00:10:12,000 --> 00:10:13,000
[Queen hisses]

199
00:10:17,000 --> 00:10:19,000
[bat squealing]

200
00:10:19,000 --> 00:10:21,000
[Queen hisses]

201
00:10:21,000 --> 00:10:24,000
[chewing]

202
00:10:27,000 --> 00:10:30,000
[Queen] Not enough. Not enough!

203
00:10:30,000 --> 00:10:33,000
I need more prey, bigger prey!

204
00:10:42,000 --> 00:10:43,000
[Kite] It's been days…

205
00:10:43,000 --> 00:10:47,000
No, it's been months
since it last rained here.

206
00:10:47,000 --> 00:10:49,000
The weather this year
has been so unstable.

207
00:10:49,000 --> 00:10:53,000
It's possible it's even
affecting the wildlife in some way,

208
00:10:53,000 --> 00:10:55,000
though it's hard to say just yet.

209
00:10:55,000 --> 00:10:57,000
So the insect with the large leg

210
00:10:57,000 --> 00:11:01,000
could be a mutation
influenced by these conditions.

211
00:11:01,000 --> 00:11:03,000
But why would it have grown larger?

212
00:11:03,000 --> 00:11:05,000
In order to survive more easily?

213
00:11:05,000 --> 00:11:06,000
If it were bigger,

214
00:11:06,000 --> 00:11:09,000
it would have a much better
chance of securing its food.

215
00:11:09,000 --> 00:11:12,000
Yeah, that's true,
but it'd need more, too, wouldn't it?

216
00:11:12,000 --> 00:11:14,000
It may be larger,

217
00:11:14,000 --> 00:11:17,000
but that doesn't always
assist in survival.

218
00:11:17,000 --> 00:11:19,000
Environment's one thing,

219
00:11:19,000 --> 00:11:22,000
but I think this is related
to the chimera ant's nature.

220
00:11:22,000 --> 00:11:25,000
[Spin] I agree.
They do reproduce in a unique way

221
00:11:25,000 --> 00:11:27,000
that isn't found in any other organism.

222
00:11:28,000 --> 00:11:29,000
They do? How?

223
00:11:29,000 --> 00:11:31,000
They reproduce
through a special process

224
00:11:31,000 --> 00:11:33,000
known as phagogenesis.

225
00:11:33,000 --> 00:11:35,000
Phagogenesis?

226
00:11:35,000 --> 00:11:36,000
What does it mean?

227
00:11:37,000 --> 00:11:40,000
[Kite] When a Chimera Ant Queen
eats other creatures,

228
00:11:41,000 --> 00:11:43,000
she's then able to impart characteristics

229
00:11:43,000 --> 00:11:46,000
of those creatures on
to the subsequent generation.

230
00:11:47,000 --> 00:11:50,000
So you see, in other words,

231
00:11:50,000 --> 00:11:53,000
ingesting multiple species
allows her to pass on

232
00:11:53,000 --> 00:11:56,000
a mix of all kinds of different
genes to her offspring.

233
00:11:58,000 --> 00:12:02,000
With each feeding,
she lays between one and five eggs.

234
00:12:02,000 --> 00:12:05,000
The first generation of births
are completely infertile,

235
00:12:05,000 --> 00:12:09,000
so they become
worker or soldier ants.

236
00:12:09,000 --> 00:12:12,000
They live their lives
in service to the queen

237
00:12:12,000 --> 00:12:16,000
as well as her eventual successors.

238
00:12:16,000 --> 00:12:17,000
Those successors

239
00:12:17,000 --> 00:12:20,000
become the king and queen
of the next generation.

240
00:12:20,000 --> 00:12:22,000
The Queen is always looking to consume

241
00:12:22,000 --> 00:12:24,000
the genes of strong organisms.

242
00:12:25,000 --> 00:12:28,000
This allows her to pass their
traits down to her offspring,

243
00:12:28,000 --> 00:12:31,000
and she may even devour
her preferred fodder species

244
00:12:31,000 --> 00:12:33,000
to its complete extinction.

245
00:12:33,000 --> 00:12:35,000
Extinction? Really?

246
00:12:35,000 --> 00:12:37,000
Yes, her appetite is voracious,

247
00:12:37,000 --> 00:12:39,000
and it can drive her
to consume her own body weight

248
00:12:39,000 --> 00:12:42,000
many times over in a single day.

249
00:12:42,000 --> 00:12:43,000
That's why Chimera Ants

250
00:12:43,000 --> 00:12:46,000
are under a designated
quarantine, level one.

251
00:12:46,000 --> 00:12:50,000
So if she sets her eyes on you,
you're finished, huh?

252
00:12:51,000 --> 00:12:53,000
Judging by the size of that claw,

253
00:12:53,000 --> 00:12:55,000
she's at least two meters long.

254
00:12:55,000 --> 00:12:58,000
That thing could eat a human
in no time at all.

255
00:12:59,000 --> 00:13:00,000
[Mon groans]

256
00:13:00,000 --> 00:13:02,000
[all groan]

257
00:13:03,000 --> 00:13:05,000
Yes, you're right about that.

258
00:13:10,000 --> 00:13:12,000
[snake hisses]

259
00:13:12,000 --> 00:13:14,000
Go away! Just stay back!

260
00:13:14,000 --> 00:13:16,000
[girl gasps] Big brother.

261
00:13:17,000 --> 00:13:19,000
It's fine. Stay close to me, Reina.

262
00:13:19,000 --> 00:13:20,000
'Kay.

263
00:13:20,000 --> 00:13:22,000
[hissing]

264
00:13:22,000 --> 00:13:25,000
[grunting softly]

265
00:13:29,000 --> 00:13:30,000
Take that!

266
00:13:32,000 --> 00:13:35,000
[snake hissing]

267
00:13:37,000 --> 00:13:39,000
[sighs]

268
00:13:39,000 --> 00:13:40,000
There. It's okay now.

269
00:13:40,000 --> 00:13:42,000
Thank you so much, big brother!

270
00:13:43,000 --> 00:13:44,000
See? I'll keep you safe.

271
00:13:44,000 --> 00:13:47,000
That's what big brothers
are for, right, Reina?

272
00:13:47,000 --> 00:13:48,000
[Reina giggles] Yep!

273
00:13:49,000 --> 00:13:51,000
Okay. Let's go home.

274
00:13:52,000 --> 00:13:55,000
[insects chirping]

275
00:13:56,000 --> 00:13:58,000
[Reina] Big brother was so amazing!

276
00:13:59,000 --> 00:14:01,000
There was this really big snake,

277
00:14:01,000 --> 00:14:04,000
but then, he was just like,
"Get outta here!"

278
00:14:05,000 --> 00:14:08,000
Now, Reina,
you shouldn't be waving your spoon around.

279
00:14:08,000 --> 00:14:10,000
That isn't very polite.

280
00:14:10,000 --> 00:14:12,000
But that's what he did, Mom.
I promise!

281
00:14:12,000 --> 00:14:14,000
I know he did, sweetie. I know.

282
00:14:15,000 --> 00:14:18,000
That was very brave,
what you did for your sister.

283
00:14:18,000 --> 00:14:20,000
If a snake that size
ever slithered up to me,

284
00:14:20,000 --> 00:14:22,000
I might be too scared to move.

285
00:14:23,000 --> 00:14:26,000
You're truly a young man now, Kurt.

286
00:14:26,000 --> 00:14:28,000
[chuckles] I guess so.

287
00:14:30,000 --> 00:14:32,000
You're already so reliable

288
00:14:33,000 --> 00:14:34,000
at only nine years old.

289
00:14:35,000 --> 00:14:39,000
And that's why I want you
to continue to look after Reina.

290
00:14:39,000 --> 00:14:42,000
I'm counting on you, Kurt.
Understand?

291
00:14:42,000 --> 00:14:44,000
[Reina] I'm counting on you, too,
big brother.

292
00:14:44,000 --> 00:14:46,000
I won't let you guys down.

293
00:14:47,000 --> 00:14:49,000
I promise that I'll keep both of you safe,

294
00:14:49,000 --> 00:14:51,000
no matter what happens, okay?

295
00:14:52,000 --> 00:14:55,000
[ominous music playing]

296
00:15:01,000 --> 00:15:04,000
[Queen] Yes. This section
is about the hatch.

297
00:15:04,000 --> 00:15:07,000
[eggs rustling]

298
00:15:20,000 --> 00:15:25,000
[Chimera Ants screech]

299
00:15:25,000 --> 00:15:27,000
[Queen] Heed me, my soldiers.

300
00:15:27,000 --> 00:15:30,000
I have a solemn duty
to give birth to the king.

301
00:15:30,000 --> 00:15:34,000
I will require large quantities
of highly nutritious food

302
00:15:34,000 --> 00:15:37,000
so that the king
will be strong and healthy,

303
00:15:37,000 --> 00:15:40,000
so go, and find me the best food you can!

304
00:15:40,000 --> 00:15:43,000
[Chimera Ants screech]

305
00:15:47,000 --> 00:15:49,000
[Queen] This section
will also hatch soon.

306
00:15:49,000 --> 00:15:53,000
I need a large nest
in which to birth the king.

307
00:15:54,000 --> 00:15:55,000
I also need rest,

308
00:15:56,000 --> 00:15:59,000
free from outside disturbances
during the pregnancy.

309
00:16:01,000 --> 00:16:04,000
If I am to birth a strong king,

310
00:16:04,000 --> 00:16:07,000
I must have strong soldiers.

311
00:16:09,000 --> 00:16:10,000
[Reina coughs]

312
00:16:11,000 --> 00:16:12,000
[coughs]

313
00:16:12,000 --> 00:16:14,000
Are you all right?

314
00:16:14,000 --> 00:16:16,000
Yeah. Thanks for asking.

315
00:16:19,000 --> 00:16:21,000
-Oh, hey. So, big brother.
-Hmm?

316
00:16:21,000 --> 00:16:24,000
One day, when I'm all grown up,

317
00:16:24,000 --> 00:16:26,000
I'm gonna get married to you.

318
00:16:26,000 --> 00:16:29,000
[chuckles] Sure.

319
00:16:29,000 --> 00:16:30,000
Hey, why don't we
wake up early tomorrow

320
00:16:31,000 --> 00:16:32,000
and go fishing at the river?

321
00:16:32,000 --> 00:16:33,000
'Kay.

322
00:16:34,000 --> 00:16:36,000
We can cook some fish for dinner.

323
00:16:36,000 --> 00:16:38,000
Mom will be so surprised.

324
00:16:39,000 --> 00:16:41,000
Yeah. Yeah, I can't wait.

325
00:16:46,000 --> 00:16:49,000
[birds chirping]

326
00:16:52,000 --> 00:16:53,000
[Reina] There are so many.

327
00:16:53,000 --> 00:16:55,000
We have enough
for a whole fish feast!

328
00:16:55,000 --> 00:16:58,000
-Yeah!
-[Reina giggles]

329
00:16:58,000 --> 00:16:59,000
[both gasp]

330
00:16:59,000 --> 00:17:02,000
[Chimera Ant chittering]

331
00:17:03,000 --> 00:17:06,000
B-big brother, what is that thing?

332
00:17:06,000 --> 00:17:08,000
[Kurt gasping]

333
00:17:10,000 --> 00:17:12,000
Help! Big brother!

334
00:17:13,000 --> 00:17:14,000
Reina, it's fine!

335
00:17:15,000 --> 00:17:17,000
[tense music playing]

336
00:17:17,000 --> 00:17:19,000
I… I'm your big brother,

337
00:17:19,000 --> 00:17:21,000
and I'll keep you safe, okay?

338
00:17:23,000 --> 00:17:26,000
I promised Mom I'd protect you!

339
00:17:26,000 --> 00:17:28,000
You're safe with me!

340
00:17:30,000 --> 00:17:31,000
Go away!

341
00:17:32,000 --> 00:17:33,000
I said go a--

342
00:17:37,000 --> 00:17:40,000
[Queen chewing]

343
00:17:40,000 --> 00:17:43,000
[Queen] This is delicious.

344
00:17:44,000 --> 00:17:46,000
And so nutritious.

345
00:17:46,000 --> 00:17:48,000
The best fodder!

346
00:17:49,000 --> 00:17:51,000
I must consume more of this species.

347
00:17:55,000 --> 00:17:58,000
[Kite] Meet Gon and Killua.
I mentioned them on the phone.

348
00:17:59,000 --> 00:18:01,000
Hello there.
My name is Lin Koshi.

349
00:18:01,000 --> 00:18:03,000
Pleasure to meet you.

350
00:18:03,000 --> 00:18:05,000
And my name is Podungo Lapoy.

351
00:18:05,000 --> 00:18:07,000
I'm happy to have you both on board.

352
00:18:08,000 --> 00:18:11,000
Glad to be here, Mr. Lin,
and you, too, Miss Podungo.

353
00:18:11,000 --> 00:18:12,000
Likewise.

354
00:18:12,000 --> 00:18:14,000
Back to business.

355
00:18:14,000 --> 00:18:15,000
So where was the leg discovered?

356
00:18:16,000 --> 00:18:18,000
On the beach right over there.

357
00:18:18,000 --> 00:18:21,000
And according to the locals here,

358
00:18:21,000 --> 00:18:24,000
one day, it just
washed up on the shore.

359
00:18:32,000 --> 00:18:35,000
Hey, there's a forest right behind us.

360
00:18:35,000 --> 00:18:39,000
Well, if it ran in there,
it'll be difficult to find it.

361
00:18:41,000 --> 00:18:44,000
We can't even be certain
that the chimera ant is still alive.

362
00:18:44,000 --> 00:18:46,000
That's a good point.

363
00:18:46,000 --> 00:18:47,000
We don't even know if it ended up

364
00:18:47,000 --> 00:18:50,000
on the same island
that its leg drifted to.

365
00:18:51,000 --> 00:18:52,000
Let's find out, then.

366
00:18:53,000 --> 00:18:54,000
[dog yips]

367
00:18:56,000 --> 00:18:58,000
Here. Just remember this scent.

368
00:18:59,000 --> 00:19:00,000
[dog whimpers]

369
00:19:00,000 --> 00:19:02,000
I can help, too!

370
00:19:02,000 --> 00:19:04,000
-Huh?
-[Gon sniffing]

371
00:19:04,000 --> 00:19:07,000
Gon's sense of smell
is just as good as a dog's.

372
00:19:07,000 --> 00:19:09,000
[sniffing]

373
00:19:11,000 --> 00:19:12,000
[Gon sniffs] Hmm.

374
00:19:26,000 --> 00:19:28,000
[Banana] Shoot.
He can't find anything.

375
00:19:28,000 --> 00:19:30,000
[Spin] I suppose the scent
may have disappeared.

376
00:19:30,000 --> 00:19:32,000
It probably rained some since then.

377
00:19:32,000 --> 00:19:34,000
[Gon] Nothing for me either.

378
00:19:34,000 --> 00:19:36,000
Guess that means
the Chimera Ant isn't here.

379
00:19:37,000 --> 00:19:41,000
We should consider the possibility
it may have washed ashore elsewhere.

380
00:19:43,000 --> 00:19:45,000
Which direction do the currents flow here?

381
00:19:45,000 --> 00:19:46,000
It's complicated.

382
00:19:46,000 --> 00:19:49,000
The direction is reversed
between day and night.

383
00:19:49,000 --> 00:19:51,000
And it changes with the seasons, too.

384
00:19:51,000 --> 00:19:53,000
It's can even be different
on certain days.

385
00:19:55,000 --> 00:19:58,000
It'll be tough
to pinpoint a precise location.

386
00:19:58,000 --> 00:20:00,000
Well, it's way too early to give up.

387
00:20:00,000 --> 00:20:02,000
Let's just split up and search.

388
00:20:02,000 --> 00:20:04,000
Good idea.

389
00:20:19,000 --> 00:20:20,000
[Gon] Still nothing.

390
00:20:20,000 --> 00:20:24,000
[Kite] It's pointless to continue
searching blindly like this.

391
00:20:24,000 --> 00:20:26,000
Let's go back to Yorknew City.

392
00:20:26,000 --> 00:20:29,000
If we're lucky, we may be able
to find a new lead to follow.

393
00:20:44,000 --> 00:20:46,000
[Killua] She's at least two meters long.

394
00:20:47,000 --> 00:20:50,000
That thing could eat a human
in no time at all.

395
00:20:52,000 --> 00:20:54,000
[Kite] A voracious appetite,

396
00:20:54,000 --> 00:20:56,000
Phagogenesis.

397
00:20:57,000 --> 00:21:00,000
[dramatic music playing]

398
00:21:14,000 --> 00:21:16,000
[Chimera Ant] My Queen.

399
00:21:16,000 --> 00:21:19,000
[Queen] Oh, you can speak, can you?

400
00:21:20,000 --> 00:21:22,000
[Chimera Ant] Yes, my Queen.
So that I may fully receive,

401
00:21:23,000 --> 00:21:25,000
understand, and execute your orders.

402
00:21:25,000 --> 00:21:27,000
[Queen] That pleases me.

403
00:21:27,000 --> 00:21:31,000
In that case, I hereby assign you
to be a squadron leader.

404
00:21:32,000 --> 00:21:33,000
[Chimera Ant] I am most grateful.

405
00:21:33,000 --> 00:21:36,000
[Queen] Now then, your first mission

406
00:21:36,000 --> 00:21:40,000
will be to lead all the soldiers
here to capture my food.

407
00:21:41,000 --> 00:21:42,000
I want you to capture

408
00:21:42,000 --> 00:21:46,000
more of those highly
nutritious organisms for me.

409
00:21:46,000 --> 00:21:47,000
[Chimera Ant] I shall.

410
00:21:57,000 --> 00:22:03,000
[narrator] And so, a Chimera Ant
has been born with human genes.

411
00:22:03,000 --> 00:22:07,000
With that, Kite's worst fears
have finally come to pass.

412
00:22:09,000 --> 00:22:12,000
[closing theme music playing]

413
00:22:12,000 --> 00:22:15,000
[singer singing in Japanese]

414
00:23:30,000 --> 00:23:32,000
[instrumental music playing]

415
00:23:35,000 --> 00:23:38,000
[Gon] Next time,
"Very rapid reproduction."

416
00:23:38,000 --> 00:23:40,000
My name is Gon Freecss!

417
00:23:40,000 --> 00:23:42,000
[Killua] My name is Killua Zoldyck.

418
00:23:42,000 --> 00:23:44,000
[both] What's your name?

419
00:23:45,000 --> 00:23:49,000
[singer singing in Japanese]
